---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **한국 팀 774개 사이에서 관심이 어떤 모양으로 퍼져 있나.** (`/attention-share`)
 *
 * ── 왜 이 지면인가 ────────────────────────────────────────────
 * 오늘 커뮤니티 씨앗(인벤 · 댓글 20): 「비인기 아이돌은 행사할때마다 적자라고 말하는 이유」
 *   ⛔ 우리는 «행사 수익»을 못 잰다. 잰 척하지 않는다.
 *   ✅ 잴 수 있는 것은 «관심의 모양»이고, 그 모양이 저 물음이 왜 생기는지를 설명한다.
 *
 * ⭐ 이슈+롱테일. 어느 팀 이야기가 돌든 이 표는 그대로 쓰인다.
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 하지 않는 것 ─────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ 열람을 「인기」로 바꿔 쓰지 않는다 — 찾아본 횟수다
 * ⛔ 🔴 열람을 «돈»으로 바꿔 쓰지 않는다. 우리는 표값도 행사비도 모른다.
 *    씨앗이 돈 이야기였으니 여기서 미끄러지기 쉽다 — 그래서 화면에 못박아 둔다
 * ⛔ 아래쪽 팀을 「실패했다」고 안 쓴다. 잰 것은 «전체의 모양»이고 한 줄이 아니다
 * ⛔ 못 잰 73팀을 0 으로 안 채운다 — 앞자료가 뺐고 그 수를 그대로 이고 간다
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import d from '../../data/kcw-attention-share.json';

const TITLE = 'How lopsided is attention on Korean acts? 24 of 774 hold half of it';

const 본 = d.본판;
const 검 = d.검산판;
const 아래팀수 = Math.ceil(본.팀수 / 2);

/* ⭐ 지면이 «셀 때마다 다시 센다». 손으로 적어 두면 자료가 바뀔 때 지면이 자기와 싸운다 */
const 몫 = (v) => (v == null ? 'not measured' : `${(Number(v) * 100).toFixed(1)}%`);
const 잔몫 = (v) => (v == null ? 'not measured' : `${(Number(v) * 100).toFixed(4)}%`);
const 수 = (n) => (n == null ? '—' : Math.round(Number(n)).toLocaleString('en-US'));
const 위키 = (t) => `https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/${encodeURIComponent(String(t).split(' ').join('_'))}`;
const 첫째 = d.위쪽스물다섯[0];
/* 두 벌이 얼마나 어긋나나 — 가장 크게 벌어진 자리를 스스로 찾아 낸다. 좋은 자리만 고르지 않는다 */
const 가장벌어진 = [...d.두벌견줌].sort((a, b) => b.차이 - a.차이)[0];
const 가장맞은 = [...d.두벌견줌].sort((a, b) => a.차이 - b.차이)[0];

const DESC =
  `In the single month ${d.잰달}, ${수(본.팀수)} Korean acts drew ${수(본.합)} English Wikipedia reads. `
  + `${본.절반가지는팀수} of them — ${몫(본.절반가지는비율)} — hold half of it, and the lower half of all acts `
  + `holds ${몫(본.아래절반몫)}. The median act was read ${수(본.가운데팀열람)} times. Not a popularity `
  + 'ranking and not a revenue figure.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  temporalCoverage: d.잰달,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://query.wikidata.org/', 'https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} page="/attention-share" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    A Korean forum thread this week asked why lesser-known idol groups are said to lose money
    on every event they play. We cannot answer that — we hold no fee, ticket or revenue data
    for any act here, and this page makes no claim about anybody's finances. What we can do is
    measure the shape of attention, and the shape is why the question exists.
  </p>

  <p>
    In the single month {d.잰달}, {수(본.팀수)} Korean music acts drew {수(본.합)} reads on
    English Wikipedia between them.{' '}<b>{본.절반가지는팀수} of those acts hold half of
    it</b>{' '}— {몫(본.절반가지는비율)} of the list. The lower half of the list, all
    {' '}{수(아래팀수)} acts together, holds {몫(본.아래절반몫)}.
  </p>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Counting down from the top</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>The most-read</th><th>Share of the month's reading</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {본.위쪽몫.map((x) => (
          <tr><td>Top {x.n} of {수(본.팀수)}</td><td>{몫(x.몫)}</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      One act — {첫째.이름} — accounts for {몫(첫째.몫)} on its own. The median act on the
      list was read {수(본.가운데팀열람)} times in the month, which is
      {' '}{잔몫(본.가운데팀몫)} of the total.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>The most-read 25</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Act</th><th>Founded</th><th>Reads in {d.잰달}</th><th>Share</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {d.위쪽스물다섯.map((t) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{t.자리}</td>
            <td><a href={위키(t.제목)} rel="nofollow">{t.이름}</a></td>
            <td>{t.데뷔해 ?? '—'}</td>
            <td>{수(t.열람)}</td>
            <td>{몫(t.몫)}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      Founding year is blank where Wikidata does not record one. It is shown because the
      list is not sorted by it and the reader can see that for themselves — the top of this
      table spans three decades of debuts.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Two separate counts, and where they disagree</h2>
    <p>
      A single month could be a fluke, so we ran the same measurement on a different act set,
      over a different window, collected separately: {수(검.팀수)} acts, act-page reads over
      twelve months. If the lopsidedness were an artefact of one month, the two would not
      match.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>The most-read</th><th>One month, {수(본.팀수)} acts</th><th>Twelve months, {수(검.팀수)} acts</th><th>Gap</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {d.두벌견줌.map((x) => (
          <tr>
            <td>Top {x.n}</td>
            <td>{몫(x.본판몫)}</td>
            <td>{몫(x.검산판몫)}</td>
            <td>{(x.차이 * 100).toFixed(1)} points</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      They agree closest at the very top — top {가장맞은.n} comes out {몫(가장맞은.본판몫)}
      {' '}against {몫(가장맞은.검산판몫)} — and drift apart further down, by up to
      {' '}{(가장벌어진.차이 * 100).toFixed(1)} points at top {가장벌어진.n}. That drift is
      expected and we would rather explain it than hide it: the twelve-month set contains
      fewer acts, so any given count of acts is a larger slice of a shorter list. What does
      not change is the finding. Both counts put roughly a tenth of everything on one act and
      about half of everything inside the top twenty.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      Stated as a single number, the one-month spread has a Gini of{' '}<b>{본.지니}</b>{' '}and
      the twelve-month spread{' '}<b>{검.지니}</b>. {d.선.지니뜻}
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>🔴 What this does not say</h2>
    <p>
      The thread that sent us here was about money, and that is exactly where a page like
      this can mislead. So, plainly: <b>a Wikipedia read is not a ticket, a stream, a fee or
      a won.</b> We have no revenue data for any act on this page. An act can be read rarely
      and tour profitably, and an act can be read constantly and lose money.
    </p>
    <p>
      What the numbers do support is narrower and still worth having. If you are the median
      act on this list, the number of people who looked you up in English in a month is
      {' '}{수(본.가운데팀열람)}. Whatever the economics of an event are, they are being
      attempted at that level of outside recognition, not at{' '}{첫째.이름}'s. The gap
      between those two conditions is what the forum thread was reaching for, and it is the
      one part of it we can put a number on.
    </p>
    {d.이것이아닌것.map((l) => <p class="note">{l}</p>)}
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Where else this leads</h2>
    <p class="note">
      The same lopsidedness turns up when we count titles instead of acts:
      {' '}<a href="/clumping">Korean titles do not spread evenly across Netflix country charts</a>{' '}
      either — they arrive nowhere for weeks and then in several places at once. And for what
      happens to an act's reading after its best month,
      {' '}<a href="/group-afterlife">the median act loses half of it in two months</a>, which
      is the other half of why the middle of this list is where it is. For where a given act's
      reading lands once it has any, see
      {' '}<a href="/member-vs-group">the group page or the member pages</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/attention-share" />

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Sources</h2>
    {d.우물.map((l) => <p class="note">{l}</p>)}
    <p class="note">
      Reads — Wikimedia Pageviews REST API, English Wikipedia, all-access,
      {' '}<b>agent=user</b>{' '}(bots excluded). Acts — Wikidata SPARQL. Neither well was
      drawn again for this page; both counts are recomputed from data we already had, so the
      two figures cannot have drifted apart through collection. Main count collected
      {' '}{d.앞자료.본판잰때}, check count {d.앞자료.검산판잰때}. Recounted {d.잰때}.
    </p>
  </section>
</WikiTip>
